# EXPECT: and the loop body WRITES it
# ouroboros#187 / EigenScript#1074: a `for` binder over a function LOCAL (or a
# fresh name, or a module name) in a function that interrogates it, where the
# loop body WRITES the binder. On the pinned VM the write is invisible to the
# next body read (prints 7 8, not 17 18) yet persists past the loop (18) --
# two answers for one binding -- so the AOT refuses rather than pick. A
# read-only body is coherent (loop-scoped) and emitted: t218. A PARAMETER
# binder is coherent since EigenScript#1063 and emitted: t116, t119.
define f(q) as:
    local r is q
    for r in [7, 8]:
        r is r + 10
        print of r
    print of r
    print of (prev of r)
    return 0
f of 1
